From 73bcd0c4d95613afcedef8280bbb615d10cb9283 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: awizardxch <awizard.eth@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:32:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Support hubs under a path prefix; prefill the hub picker from
 ?hub=

A hub may now be served under a path (https://host.example/hub/a), as
behind a reverse proxy or an embedding host that maps one path per server,
such as a Discord Activity URL mapping.

- New front-end/src/services/hubUrl.ts: canonicalHubUrl (a root hub stays
  its bare origin, so existing session credentials are unchanged; a path
  hub keeps its path) and hubResourceUrl.
- The lobby iframe and /ws/game resolve under the hub URL. Session
  credentials derive from the hub URL, so two hubs on one origin get
  different sessions. The hub picker keeps the path.
- hub-frontend resolves ws/hub against its own page URL.
- build-meta.json is fetched page-relative and basePath is relative
  (app/<nonce>/), so the same stage serves at a root or under a prefix.
  isStaleDeploy, verify-stage and verify-deploy-archives follow.
- ?hub=<url> prefills the hub picker. It never connects on its own: a
  link must not be able to put a player on a hub.

Tests: hub_url.test.ts pins the pre-change credentials for root hubs;
picker, credential and deployFreshness tests cover paths. An end-to-end
run behind a prefix-stripping proxy matched two players and delivered
advisory_start over /hub/bow/ws/game; the same run at a hub root passed.
